    <ns4:acronym xml:lang="en">BLBSev</ns4:acronym>
    <ns1:definition xml:lang="en">Wheat bacterial leaf blight severity in the plants caused by the agent Pseudomonas syringae pv. syringae. symptoms: small (less than 0.04 inches) water-soaked lesions expand and eventually coalesce. initial lesions become necrotic and turn from gray-green to tan-white. Entire leaves may become necrotic, but heads and glumes are typically symptomless.</ns1:definition>
