    <ns1:definition xml:lang="en">Sampling for water soluble carbohydrate is often combined with in-season biomass sampling and partitioning. Ensure to plan sampling approach carefully to allow for maximal data collection/economy of sampling (e.g., data on partitioning weights can be collected on the same 20 culm sample). The leaf lamina and/or leaf sheath may also be analyzed for WSC separately, or not removed from the stem for ?whole stem? analysis. Lab analysis is performed by NIR or wet chemical method.</ns1:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://cropontology.org/rdf/Measurement"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">StmWSC Measurement</rdfs:label>
  </ns2:Class>
